'''adorn''' (a̤-dôrn′), ''v. t.'' [< ME. ''adornen'', ''adournen'', < OF. ''adorner'', ''adourner'' (earlier ME. ''aournen'', ''aornen'', < OF. ''aourner'', ''aürner'', ''aörner''), mod. F. ''adorner'' = Sp. Pg. ''adornar'' = It. ''adornare'', < L. ''adornare'', < ''ad'', to, + ''ornare'', deck, beautify: see

